Appendix F: Simulation Algorithms

F.1 Deterministic Simulation

```
Input: α, κ, ρ, g_C, g_T, x_0, p_0, T
Output: trajectory { (x_t, p_t) }_{t=0}^T

for t = 0 to T-1:
    ΔS = p_t * g_C - (1 - p_t) * g_T
    x_{t+1} = x_t + α * x_t * (1 - x_t) * ΔS
    p_{t+1} = p_t + κ * x_t * (1 - p_t) - ρ * (1 - x_t) * p_t
    clamp x_{t+1} to [0,1]
    clamp p_{t+1} to [0,1]
end
```

F.2 Stochastic Simulation

```
Input: N, α, κ, ρ, g_C, g_T, x_0, p_0, T
Output: trajectory { (x_t, n_t) }_{t=0}^T

n_0 = round(p_0 * N)
for t = 0 to T-1:
    p_t = n_t / N
    ΔS = p_t * g_C - (1 - p_t) * g_T
    x_{t+1} = x_t + α * x_t * (1 - x_t) * ΔS
    clamp x_{t+1} to [0,1]
    
    // Moran process step
    T_up = κ * x_{t+1} * (1 - p_t) * p_t + κ * x_{t+1} * (1 - p_t)^2
    T_down = ρ * (1 - x_{t+1}) * p_t * (1 - p_t) + ρ * (1 - x_{t+1}) * p_t^2
    T_stay = 1 - T_up - T_down
    
    draw u ~ Uniform(0,1)
    if u < T_up:
        n_{t+1} = n_t + 1
    elif u < T_up + T_down:
        n_{t+1} = n_t - 1
    else:
        n_{t+1} = n_t
    clamp n_{t+1} to [0,N]
end
```

F.3 Parameter Ranges for Phase Diagrams

Typical ranges for simulation:

· \alpha \in [0.01, 0.5]
· \kappa \in [0.01, 0.5]
· \rho \in [0.01, 0.5]
