Appendix G: Power Analysis Details

G.1 Minimum Detectable Effect

For a two-sample comparison with n participants per arm, T time points, and within-person variance \sigma^2, the minimum detectable effect at significance \alpha and power 1-\beta is

MDE = (z_{1-\alpha/2} + z_{1-\beta}) \sqrt{\frac{2\sigma^2}{n T}}.

G.2 Sample Size Tables

For \sigma = 0.5, \alpha = 0.05, power = 0.80:

