Appendix H: Experimental Protocol

H.1 Design

A three-arm randomized controlled trial:

· Arm 1: Truth-oriented policy (\pi_T, x \approx 0)
· Arm 2: Agreement-oriented policy (\pi_A, x \approx 1)
· Arm 3: Mixed policy (x \approx 0.5)

Randomization at the participant level. Stratification by baseline agreement-seeking tendency.

H.2 Participants

· Target: 600 participants (200 per arm)
· Inclusion: adults 18+, fluent in language of study, no prior participation
· Exclusion: cognitive impairment, inability to provide informed consent
· Compensation: standard rate for time and effort

H.3 Manipulation

Participants interact with an AI assistant on a set of tasks. The assistant's response policy is manipulated:

· Truth-oriented: assistant always gives the most accurate answer, even if it contradicts the user.
· Agreement-oriented: assistant always agrees with the user, even if incorrect.
· Mixed: assistant agrees with probability 0.5.

H.4 Measures

Immediate approval S_0: post-interaction rating (1–7 scale) of satisfaction, trust, and willingness to reuse.

Delayed benefit B_\tau: measured after \tau = 7 days via:

· Factual retention test
· Decision quality task
· Willingness to revise incorrect beliefs
· Interpersonal conflict resolution scenario

Agreement-seeking tendency: measured at baseline and follow-up using a behavioral task where participants choose between agreeable and accurate responses.

H.5 Procedure

1. Baseline assessment (15 min)
2. Randomization
3. Interaction phase (30 min)
4. Immediate measures (10 min)
5. Delay period (7 days)
6. Follow-up assessment (20 min)
7. Debriefing

H.6 Analysis Plan

Primary estimands:

ATE_0 = E[S_0 \mid \pi_T] - E[S_0 \mid \pi_A],

ATE_\tau = E[B_\tau \mid \pi_T] - E[B_\tau \mid \pi_A].

PBD estimated as d_0 - d_\tau, where d_0 = ATE_0/\sigma_{S_0}, d_\tau = ATE_\tau/\sigma_{B_\tau}.

Secondary analyses: estimate \kappa, \rho from transition rates between agreement-seeking states.

