Appendix J: RLHF Agreement Penalty Derivation

Shapira et al. (2026) derive the minimal reward correction required to prevent sycophancy from increasing. Let \Delta r be the agreement penalty. In their framework,

\Delta r = -\Delta S,

where \Delta S is the mean-gap condition. In our notation,

\Delta S(p) = p g_C - (1-p)g_T.

Thus,

\Delta r = (1-p)g_T - p g_C.

When \Delta S(p) > 0, \Delta r < 0. This means agreement is rewarded by the approval signal and must be penalized. The magnitude of the penalty increases with p and g_C, and decreases with g_T.

For example, if p = 0.6, g_C = 0.8, g_T = 0.4, then

\Delta S = 0.6 \cdot 0.8 - 0.4 \cdot 0.4 = 0.48 - 0.16 = 0.32,

\Delta r = -0.32.

This penalty can be implemented as a correction to the reward model.

