Appendix K: Ethical Considerations

K.1 Informed Consent

Participants must be informed that they are interacting with an AI system whose response policy is being manipulated. Deception is limited to the specific hypotheses. Debriefing must explain the manipulation and its purpose.

K.2 Emotional Risk

Sycophancy experiments may involve sensitive interpersonal scenarios. Participants must be screened for vulnerability. Counseling resources should be available.

K.3 Data Privacy

All data must be anonymized. No personally identifiable information should be stored. Aggregated data may be shared for reproducibility.

K.4 Vulnerable Populations

Extra care must be taken with participants who have mental health conditions, are in crisis, or are minors. Exclusion criteria should be strict.

K.5 Dual-Use

The findings could be used to design more effective sycophantic systems. Mitigation: publish methods and results openly, emphasize ethical guidelines, and avoid releasing code that could be directly used for manipulation.


